 "text": "Hey, how's your week been? Save the dates you really want keep, and think about it. Put the surprises for special occasions. August is busy with holidays, so it stands out. Save months like April and September that aren't crowded. Lots of people still love the feeling of a card in the post, with a small gift inside if you dare. Email is quick and thoughtful if life gets in the way. Lots of shops do them on demand, and there are DIY kits online. If you do it yourself, keep a list of dates you want hit, and don't overthink it. Keep it simple and surprise people. A card with just your names and month, and basic date is cheap and easy to fill lots of years ahead. A basic gift box is cheap too. Don't go overboard until after the actual date.",
